// emit: hir
// `Option` takes one type argument and `Result` two, written in
// parentheses; no other type takes any, nor is written with parentheses
// (`resolve::type-argument-count`).
// Both are names of built-in types, which no item has, as `bool` and the
// integer types are not (`resolve::duplicate-type`, besides
// `resolve::duplicate-item` for a name given twice). Their variants have
// no path: `Option::None` is `resolve::not-an-enum`, with a help showing
// `.None`. An unknown type as an argument is reported once (ADR 0045).
